# Sürüm notları (“new version”)

When the user says **new version** (or **yeni sürüm**), add a staff release note. Do not wait for them to mention changelog.

## Scope

Write one nutshell of **everything shipped for staff since the previous “new version” in this conversation** (or since the last `STAFF_CHANGELOG` entry if this chat has none). Include features **and** bug fixes. Skip unfinished or reverted work. Do not dump file lists.

## How to publish

1. Edit `src/lib/staffChangelog.js` only (unless they ask otherwise).
2. **Insert a new object at the top** of `STAFF_CHANGELOG`. Never edit an old `id` in place — seen notes stay dismissed.
3. New `id`: `YYYY-MM-DD-short-slug` (today’s date). Must be unique.
4. Copy is **Turkish**, same voice as existing notes: short `title`, `summary`, optional `steps` for how to find it in the panel.
5. Set `roles` on the entry or on items (`director`, `teacher`, `counselor`) so people only see what applies to them.
6. Parents do not see these notes.

## Example shape

```js
{
  id: '2026-09-08-atlas-classes',
  title: 'Kısa başlık',
  publishedOn: '2026-09-08',
  intro: 'Bir cümlelik özet.',
  items: [
    {
      title: 'Ne değişti',
      summary: 'Personelin bilmesi gereken etki.',
      steps: ['Yönetim → …'],
      roles: ['director'],
    },
  ],
}
```
